{"name":"Carmelite","hex":"#b98970","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Carmelite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the Order of the Brothers of Our Lady of Mount Carmel, a Catholic religious order focusing on contemplative prayer and the Virgin Mary.","A variety of pear."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or related to the Carmelites."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Carmelite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carmelites","blocks":[{"text":"The Order of the Brothers of the Blessed Virgin Mary of Mount Carmel, known as the Carmelites or sometimes by synecdoche known simply as Carmel, is a mendicant order in the Catholic Church for both men and women. Historical records about its origin remain uncertain; it was probably founded in the 12th century on Mount Carmel in the Holy Land."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/66/Carmelites_OCarm_Official_Crest_Logo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carmelites"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Elias%27_Himmelfahrt-DSC2080.jpg/500px-Elias%27_Himmelfahrt-DSC2080.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Elias%27_Himmelfahrt-DSC2080.jpg/1280px-Elias%27_Himmelfahrt-DSC2080.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Elias%27_Himmelfahrt-DSC2080.jpg/500px-Elias%27_Himmelfahrt-DSC2080.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Prophet Elijah (here  ascending to heaven while Elisha is looking on, 14th-century glass window) is regarded as the spiritual father of the Carmelite order.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElias'_Himmelfahrt-DSC2080.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org